      <image:title>Where I Live</image:title>
      <image:caption>People often ask me why I keep talking about Chatt El Salem.

Why do I keep photographing this beach? Why put so much time and energy into documenting what happens here?

Because I live here.

This is our house . From the beach, I can see our house beyond the oasis — a landscape I have known all my life.

Maybe that is why I cannot simply look away.

When I photograph Chatt El Salem beach I am not photographing a distant environmental issue. I am photographing home.

And when you see your own home being threatened, documenting it becomes more than photography.</image:caption>
    </image:image>
