      <image:title>Who Was Destroyed and Who Destroyed</image:title>
      <image:caption>A small fishing boat lies abandoned on the sand, its nets strewn and forsaken in the sand. On the horizon, a huge cargo ship passes by, carrying fertiliser from the chemical complex that has depleted this sea.

This boat was not always on the sand. It knew the water, and the water knew it. The nets used to be full, and the fisherman would return before dawn with a sufficient catch. This trade was a legacy passed down from father to son, from hand to hand, from sea to sea.

Today, the boat does not move. The nets do not catch anything. And the huge ship passes indifferently on the horizon, carrying the complex’s produce and sailing on.
</image:caption>
